jd_excerpt:
It all started when engineer Fred Luddy wrote code that automated a tedious task for his coworker, Phyllis. She cried tears of joy. That moment inspired Fred to build a company that could do that for everyone—freeing people from busywork so they could focus on meaningful work. Today, ServiceNow is the AI control tower for business reinvention. Our ServiceNow AI platform brings together any AI, any data, and any workflow— helping 85% of the Fortune 500® work smarter, faster, and better. We're building an AI-native culture where technology and talent are unstoppable together. And we're just getting started.
 Join us to put AI to work for people.
 &#xa0;
What you get to do in this role: 
 This is a hands-on senior product leadership role for Autonomous Data Analytics, which ServiceNow launched at Knowledge 2026 alongside Context Engine and Workflow Data Fabric as part of a real-time data foundation for autonomous AI. The person in this role owns the product direction for the offering and makes day-to-day decisions about what to build, how to price and package it, and where to invest. The role is built around making decisions from evidence, especially product usage data, and keeping customers at the center of those decisions.&#xa0;
 The role works across many teams. In a given week you may be working with product managers, engineering, design, product marketing, sales, customer success, finance, and partners, often on several initiatives at once.&#xa0;
 Key Responsibilities&#xa0;
 Day-to-day product decisions: Make and communicate prioritization, scope, and tradeoff decisions for Autonomous Data Analytics. Decide quickly with the information available, and revisit decisions when new evidence comes in.&#xa0;
 Usage-driven decisions: Review adoption and usage data regularly. Use it to decide what to build, fix, promote, or retire, and to find where specific customer segments aren’t getting value. Turn raw data into clear recommendations for product, engineering, and leadership.&#xa0;
 Pricing and packaging: Own the pricing and packaging strategy for the offering. Define editions, entitlements, and bundles with finance, sales, and go-to-market teams. Model how packaging choices affect adoption, expansion, and deal economics, and use usage data to test those assumptions. Be able to explain the reasoning behind packaging decisions to sellers and customers.&#xa0;
 Customer focus: Stay close to customers. Review feedback, join customer calls where possible, and bring specific customer examples into product decisions. Make sure the roadmap reflects the problems customers are trying to solve.&#xa0;
 Roadmap and execution: Own the multi-release roadmap for the offering, manage dependencies with platform groups such as Context Engine, Workflow Data Fabric, and AI Control Tower, and resolve priority conflicts between teams.&#xa0;
 Cross-team work: Build alignment across teams that you don’t fully control, using shared metrics, clear priorities, and transparent tradeoffs.&#xa0;
 Product management team: Support and develop the product managers on the offering through coaching, clear expectations, and regular feedback on their decisions.&#xa0;
 Go-to-market and adoption: Work with product marketing, product success, sales, and partners on launch plans and adoption programs. Use usage and deal data to decide where adoption effort goes.&#xa0;
 Governance and responsible AI: Work with engineering, legal, and risk partners to make sure the data and AI capabilities in the offering meet governance standards.&#xa0;
To be successful in this role you have: 
 12+ years of product management or product leadership experience, with a strong focus on analytics, business intelligence, or data platforms&#xa0;
 At least 5 years in senior leadership roles at a SaaS, enterprise software, or enterprise AI company, where the work centered on data and analytics products&#xa0;
 Hands-on experience shipping analytics, BI, or data platform products to enterprise customers&#xa0;
 Demonstrated interest in and experience with pricing and packaging, including building or changing editions, entitlements, or consumption-based models, and working through the effect on deals and customer adoption&#xa0;
 Hands-on experience using product usage and telemetry data to make prioritization and packaging decisions. You can name the metrics you used, how you measured them, and what changed as a result.&#xa0;
 Customer-facing experience with enterprise customers, including gathering requirements, handling escalations, or presenting product direction&#xa0;
 Experience leading product work across multiple teams at the same time&#xa0;
 Understanding of AI/ML fundamentals, including how data quality and governance affect AI outcomes&#xa0;
 Ability to explain complex data, platform, and commercial topics clearly to executives, engineers, sellers, and customers&#xa0;
 Preferred Qualifications&#xa0;
 Experience with SaaS pricing models such as subscription tiers, consumption, or hybrid models, and with how AI capabilities are priced&#xa0;
 Experience with product analytics tools and usage metrics (funnel, cohort, and retention analysis)&#xa0;
 Background in data governance, data quality, or metadata management&#xa0;
 Experience in enterprise workflow, ITSM, or operational platforms&#xa0;
 Comfort operating in matrixed organizations with many stakeholders&#xa0;
 What Success Looks Like&#xa0;
 The offering has a packaging model that customers and sellers understand, and that is backed by adoption and deal data.&#xa0;
 Product decisions are made quickly and can be traced to usage data and customer evidence.&#xa0;
 Low-adoption capabilities are identified early and either fixed, repositioned, or retired.&#xa0;
 Customers can describe how the offering has improved their work, and their feedback is visible in the roadmap.&#xa0;
 Autonomous Data Analytics shows a clear adoption trajectory.&#xa0;
